    "created_at": "2026-06-22T22:20:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-22T22:28:22Z",
    "body": "I think the missing piece is that while the actual javascript URL navigation is queued, the ongoing navigation ID is set synchronously.\n\nBut ah, you're right on the timing front. This does seem to work by accident with regard to timing of task queues. If the queued javascript: task runs before the planned form navigation task calls [navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate) and replaces that ongoing navigation ID, then it won’t be cancelled.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
